    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "2 Viking Wharf is a well-presented three-bedroom townhouse situated in the popular Viking Wharf development, conveniently located within easy reach of Kinsale town centre."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Extending to 122.4 sq. m., this spacious home offers well-proportioned and versatile accommodation arranged over three floors, with a further ground floor level providing excellent additional living space.\r\n\r\nThe ground floor comprises an entrance hall, bathroom, utility room and a generous study/games room, offering a versatile space that could be used as a home office, playroom or additional reception room.\r\n\r\nOn the first floor, the property benefits from a bright and spacious open-plan kitchen, dining and living area, providing an ideal setting for both everyday living and entertaining. The generous living room is complemented by a well-appointed kitchen and dining area, creating a practical and contemporary main living space.\r\n\r\nThe second floor comprises two bedrooms and a family bathroom, while the top floor is dedicated to the spacious master bedroom, complete with ensuite bathroom.\r\n\r\nThe property is presented in good condition throughout and is ready for immediate occupation, while also offering scope for modernisation and for a new owner to put their own stamp on the accommodation.\r\n\r\nCommunal off-street parking is available close to the house, while heating is provided by an electric heating system.\r\n\r\nViking Wharf is ideally positioned close to Kinsale town centre, with its wide selection of shops, cafés, restaurants, bars and local amenities all within easy reach. The development also provides convenient access to the surrounding coastline and the many recreational amenities Kinsale has to offer.\r\n\r\nWith its generous accommodation, flexible additional living space, excellent location and scope for modernisation, 2 Viking Wharf represents an attractive opportunity to acquire a spacious three-bedroom home in Kinsale."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Stunning views across Kinsale Harbour, estuary and Castlepark Marina.\r\nJust minutes walk from Kinsale town centre"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: C"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Location",
        "SortOrder": 10,
        "Content": "Viking Wharf is a fine town house with breathtaking views overlooking Kinsale Harbour, estuary and Castlepark Marina.\r\n\r\nThis area of South West Ireland is of outstanding beauty with its dramatic coastline, unspoilt locations and safe beaches. Leisure activities are well catered for, Kinsale provides excellent sailing, yachting and fishing facilities from its two marinas. There are three world class golf courses including the renowned Old Head of Kinsale. Other recreational pursuits include walking, bathing, surfing, and horse riding.\r\n\r\nThere are numerous cultural events held throughout the year, such as the world famous Kinsale Arts Festival, the Cork Jazz Festival, Cork Film Festival, Kinsale Gourmet Festival along with a thriving music and opera programme. Cork has several fine theatres, and Cork Opera House hosts many exceptional productions throughout the year. Kinsale is also home to some of Ireland’s finest restaurants, contributing to its title as Gourmet Capital of Ireland; along with many top class hotels and welcoming pubs.\r\n\r\nCork International Airport is conveniently located 20 minutes drive from Kinsale with direct links within Ireland and to major European and UK cities."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Disclaimer/Privacy Policy:",
        "SortOrder": 10,
        "Content": "Finest International Real Estate Ireland Ltd. t/a Engel & Voelkers act as agents for the vendors or lessors of this property whose agents they are, give notice that: \r\n1. By sending an enquiry through the property portal in relation to any of our property listings you are consenting to the storage, use and processing of your personal data by the provider according to Engel & Voelkers’ privacy policy in order for us to reply to your contact request or request for information. A copy of our privacy policy can be viewed at www.engelvoelkers.com/southkerry/privacypolicy. You can revoke your consent at any time in the future in line with the privacy policy.\r\n2. The particulars are set out as a general outline for the guidance of intending purchasers or lessees, and do not institute, nor constitute part of, an offer or contract. \r\n3. All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition and necessary permissions for use and occupation, and any other details are given in good faith and are believed to be correct, but any intending purchasers or tenants should not rely on them as statements or representatives of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each of them. \r\n4. Any loose furniture, non-integrated appliances, white goods and curtains are deemed not to be included in the sale of the property unless specifically agreed between the parties and outlined in an inventory. Any reference to appliances refers to integrated appliances only.\r\n5. No person in the employment of Finest International Real Estate Ireland Ltd. t/a Engel & Voelkers has any authority to make or give representation or warranty in relation to this property. \r\n6. Availability upon agreement - subject to contract. This offer is subject to change of price, withdrawal or prior sale without notice. \r\n7. Transfer fees, i.e. stamp duty, solicitor fees etc, are not included in the sales price and have to be paid by the buyer. The commission will be paid by the seller."
